<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns A to Thailand's samurai bonds.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns A to Thailand's samurai bonds.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp (S&amp;P) said on Wednesday that it had assigned an A rating to Thailand's two separate samurai bond issues totalling 30 billion yen.</p>
<p>The rating was assigned to Thailand's 15 billion yen 1.85 percent samurai bond due December 7, 2001, as well as its 15 billion yen 2.85 percent samurai bond due December 20, 2006.</p>
<p>The outlook is stable, S&amp;P said in a statement.</p>
</text>
